1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,671
At my grandmother's house, the day always began before the sun.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:09,675
She spreads fresh grass on the floor.

3
00:00:09,675 --> 00:00:11,459
It is how she says:

4
00:00:11,459 --> 00:00:13,431
you are welcome here.

5
00:00:13,531 --> 00:00:16,638
Green beans go onto the pan.

6
00:00:16,638 --> 00:00:22,962
Smoke rises, and the whole street knows coffee is coming.

7
00:00:23,062 --> 00:00:28,850
She carries the smoke around the room, slowly.

8
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:32,373
Nothing here is ever rushed.

9
00:00:32,473 --> 00:00:36,131
Then the beans are ground by hand.

10
00:00:36,131 --> 00:00:39,144
I used to count the strokes.

11
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:43,417
The clay pot sits on the charcoal.

12
00:00:43,417 --> 00:00:44,344
We wait.

13
00:00:44,344 --> 00:00:47,824
Waiting is part of the coffee.

14
00:00:47,924 --> 00:00:55,315
She pours in one long, thin line, and not one drop spills.

15
00:00:55,415 --> 00:00:58,378
Neighbours come, one by one.

16
00:00:58,378 --> 00:01:00,070
Nobody asks why.

17
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:04,726
The smoke of frankincense is the invitation.

18
00:01:04,826 --> 00:01:06,574
Three rounds.

19
00:01:06,574 --> 00:01:13,297
The first abol, the second tuna, the third bereka.

20
00:01:13,397 --> 00:01:16,939
I have learned much since.

21
00:01:16,939 --> 00:01:22,253
But I still know the sound of patience:

22
00:01:22,253 --> 00:01:26,068
a clay pot, quietly singing.
